  "response": "{\"campaign_title\": \"Fragments of the Void\",\n\"campaign_subtitle\": \"The Drift Between Stars\",\n\"campaign_logline\": \"A desperate pilot navigates a fractured trade route and unravels a web of corporate interests, smuggling secrets in the shadow of the shadow-gate network.\",\n\"campaign_pitch\": \"In the wake of a dying sun's energy crisis, humanity has retreated to the jump-gates. The Zenith Corporation aims for order through monopoly, training on the Aurelia trade guilds and finding solace in the Vanguard's militaristic pride. You are not a hero; you are a scavenger seeking enough fuel for tomorrow's flight. Navigate the politics of three warring factions while your local broker, Kaelen, feeds you contracts that seem increasingly specific.\",\n\"campaign_story_summary\": \"The sector is currently in a 'Stasis Lock' because the jump-gates have become volatile and unstable. A cargo ship was recently destroyed near Gate 42. While Zenith owns the most stable gates, they are hoarding resources. The Aurelia trade guilds are desperate for raw materials, to keep their gates open. The Vanguard takes no sides in security; they only want tos secure clear corridors for military maneuvers. You start with a relic of a ship and just need to get paid.\",\n\"tone\": \"Dry, gritty frontier humor. Desarcaded, slightly cynical about the corporate-heavy void.\",\n\"opening\":\n  {\n    \"status_quo\": \"The jump-gates are humming with radiation. The 'Void-Sickness' is a real threat to every pilot. You sit in as cabin of a patched-up freighter, listening to get even a single scrap of metal worth salvage.\",\n    \"visible_crisis\": \"Gate 42 has been offline for three days. Gate 43 is flickering and unstable. The local trade routes are being choked by 'Reaver' ships - piraticalerates that appear suddenly from the shadows of the harder-gates.\",\n    \"hidden_crisis\": \"The jump-gates are not just malfunctioning; they are reacting to something in the deep void, something that isn't supposed to be there. The gate network is pulsing with a rhythmic pulse that only a few know how to interpret.\",\n  \"why_now\": \"A massive solar flare and a power surge during the transition between Gate 42 and 43 are causing gates to collapse into 'dead zones', creating a niche for smugglers and desperate traders who can navigate these dead zones.\",\n  \"player_role\": \"You start as an independent pilot with no affiliations. You have a bullseye on your back from the space pirates, pirates and the three main factions. They all want something different from you because they are willing to work outside of their established protocols.\"\n  },\n\"mystery\":\n  {\n    \"question\": \"Why is Gate 42's signal being repeated by a stranger?\",\"false_answer\": \"The gate's signal is just malfunctioning due to radiation.\",\n    \"true_answer_hint\": \"The signal is not a single pulse, but an echo of something much deeper in the space-form\",\n  \"long_term_reveal_direction\": \"Depending on your choices, you might find evidence that the gates are reacting to a narrative and not just a100% mechanical failure.\"\n  },\n\"kaelen\":\n  {\n    \"public_role\": \"Broker, Fixer, and Contract Handler.\",\n    \"secret_angle\": \"Kaelen knows the gate network's true origin and its deep-shft. She is not a scientist or a100% official; she just seems to feel 'tuned' to it.\",\n    \"address_rule\": \"She may refer to your contracts as 'opportunities for growth' or 'fetch me something.'\",\n    \"never_reveal_rule\": \"Her mystery remains intact. She never speaks of the other dimensions, are not a single prophet, she is always just the fixer.\"\n  },\n  \"factions\":\n  {\n    \"zenith_problem\": \"Zenith wants to secure every gate and monopolize the rest. They want you to do the 'dirty work' of clearing pirates.\",\n    \"aurelia_problem\": \"Aurelia trade guilds are desperate for materials. They are only interested in your cargo, not your politics.\",\n    \"vanguard_problem\": \"Vanguard is a cracked-hard military force. They want you to clear the paths and ensure they are way out of reach.\",\n  \"conflict_triangle\": \"Zenith wants the gate-link; Aurelia is trying to find a piece of it; Vanguard takes no sides but demands security.\",\n  \"neutral_space_pressure\": \"The Reaver pirates are a growing threat. They can't be told where they can't go, and they'll attack you if they are near them.\"\n  },\n  \"act_1\":\n  {\n    \"name\": \"The Broken Circuit\",\n    \"goal\": \"Navigate the local sector to find a few pieces of scrap metal and reach Gate 42.\",\n    \"opening_incident\": \"You receive a contract from Kaelen to retrieve a sensor-array from a derelict ship near Gate 42.\",\n    \"midpoint_turn\": \"While traveling to the gate, you encounter an 'Reaver' pirate ship. You must defeat it and then find the turn-off. They don't know who you can't be they are just looking for a way out.\",\n  \"finale\":\n  \"The player finds a piece of data-core from the rest of a derelict ship, but rather than than a more complex plot, the player is simply rewarded with enough credits to pay off their fuel costs and pay thes 100% certainty that they are not 'chosen'.\",\n  \"player_takeaway\": \"The sense of being an independent pilot in a dangerous space-s_core. The feeling of the gate network's instability is palpable. You learn to navigate the cracked-cracked corridors between gates.\"\n  },\n  \"starter_mission\":\n  {\n    \"title\": \"First Contact with the Reaver\",\n    \"reason\": \"Kaelen gives you a piece of cargo and a simple task: find it in your way. You must engage and defeat one Reaver-like ship.\",\n    \"enemy_identity\": \"A single, pirate-style 'Reaver' scout. It is not a player choice; it is a hard-coded first mission.\",\n    \"enemy_knows\": \"The enemy does not know who you are. They just want to clear the path ands defend their territory.\",\n  \"aftershock\": \"After defeating thes Reaver, you find a scrap",
